    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d779">

                <pb facs="0829" n="817" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg817"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">825.20/152: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-06T17:00:00-04:00">March 6, 1943—5 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>258. Your 315, February 18, 6 p.m.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d779-f1"/> Navy
                    Department states that during the recent visits to Valparaiso of Rear Admiral
                    Whiting he conferred with the Chief of the General Staff of the Chilean
                        Navy<anchor n="52" xml:id="d779-f2"/> and reached several agreements for
                    cooperative action. These agreements provide for the designation of an American
                    liaison officer with the General Staff and for two Chilean Naval Officers to be
                    received on vessels of the Southeast Pacific Force.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
